# self-healing loop crontab for user `joblander` (JOB-731 Phase 2).
# Installed WHOLESALE by init/init.sh: `crontab -u joblander <this file>` —
# it owns the entire crontab; hand edits on the VM are lost on re-init.
#
# Legacy reference: deploy/cron/joblander-agents.crontab.snapshot (old VM, as-found).

# The TS watcher's notify.sh lives in the workspace clone on the NEW VM layout
# (default inside the watcher still points at the legacy /home/joblander/joblander/... path).
WATCH_NOTIFY_SCRIPT=/home/joblander/workspace/scripts/notify.sh

# Watcher tick (JOB-670): product-output pager, every minute.
# The `&& gcloud logging write ...` chain ships the heartbeat to Cloud Logging
# ONLY on exit 0 — a crashed tick writes no heartbeat, which is exactly what
# the Terraform dead-man alert (WATCHER_HEARTBEAT absent 5 min) catches.
# Log id `self-healing-watcher` must match var.heartbeat_log_id in
# infra/terraform/modules/self-healing-vm/variables.tf.
#
# --- ROLE HANDED OVER (TEST-PLAN stage 3, 2026-07-16): this VM is the LIVE
# pager; the legacy VM's watcher cron line is commented out. Stage 4 (2026-07-17):
# trigger targets THIS VM's dispatcher (default localhost:4100) — full loop local.
* * * * * cd /home/joblander/self-healing/watcher && /usr/bin/node dist/tick.js >> /home/joblander/output-watch.log 2>&1 && gcloud logging write self-healing-watcher "WATCHER_HEARTBEAT tick ok" --severity=INFO >/dev/null 2>&1

# Hourly monitor session (error-side triage; runs from the workspace clone —
# run-monitor-session.sh sources scripts/lib/agent-launcher.sh next to it).
# --- ROLE HANDED OVER (stage 3M, 2026-07-17): this VM runs the hourly monitor;
# the legacy VM's hourly cron is commented out. State (teams/logs/monitoring)
# was copied from the legacy VM before handover. Runs from THIS repo.
0 * * * * systemd-cat -t joblander-monitor /home/joblander/self-healing/monitor/run-monitor-session.sh

# --- CWS crons: ENABLED AT CUTOVER (Phase 4) ---------------------------------
# The legacy joblander-agents VM still runs these; enabling here too would
# double-run them. Uncomment only on the owner's cutover signal.
# 0 8 * * * /home/joblander/cws-recon/run.sh >> /home/joblander/cws-recon/cron.log 2>&1
# 5 8 * * 1 bash /home/joblander/workspace/scripts/run-cws-metrics.sh >> /home/joblander/workspace/reports/cws-rankings/cron.log 2>&1
